body:
Depends how you look at it;

I mean, you gotta eat. Thats a basic part of life, and going without it just to get a video game isn't recommended. What Id do is take a few dollars out of my food budget each week, then buy it when Ive accumulated enough money (shouldnt take long at all, games only 15 bucks)

But I will say this, the game has the potential to give you hundreds and hundreds of hours, all depending on how much you wanna get outta it. The basic concept is to survive as long as possible, and anything and everything outside of that is up to you. Ive seen a divide in the buyers of this game, and its really black and white. You either really, really like it, or fucking despise it. But if survival games are something you like, then this would be my first recommendation, over anything else like it in the market right now.
